      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For wind-damaged roof repairs in Utah, local contractors like Frame Restoration Utah provide 24/7 emergency tarping and insurance claim documentation.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Frame Restoration Utah"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Steps After Wind Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Loose materials and wet decking create severe safety risks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document everything: Take clear ground-level photos of missing shingles, debris, or dented flashing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent further leaks: Request emergency roof tarping to protect your interior from incoming weather."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule an inspection: Contact a licensed local professional to check bond lines and lifted sealant that cannot be seen from the driveway."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Types of Wind Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Torn or missing shingles: High gusts break shingle seal strips and peel them back."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Creased shingles: Wind can bend a shingle back down so it looks fine, but the broken seal leaves it loose and vulnerable to the next storm."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flashing failures: Strong winds loosen metal work around chimneys, valleys, and roof vents, creating entry points for water."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Could you tell me your city or general area in Utah and whether you have an active roof leak right now so I can find the closest available repair crew for you?"
